From 7ca857f7c46da3ec06ae2d9741b49e8fa1edc7a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: greyoak111 <suny96636@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:46:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Test the floating chat against a "Hide OBS" capture of its
 own

The floating chat test used the profile's screen capture as the "Hide OBS"
case, but that source may not hide OBS at all, and it compared brightness,
which a dark desktop behind the dark chat cannot tell apart. Test both modes
with temporary captures that set "Hide OBS" explicitly, compare pixels, and
also check that LiveHime's other windows, and one opened afterwards, stay
out of a "Hide OBS" capture while the chat is allowed in.

The test README now asks for development builds only: a build sharing the
installed app's bundle id takes over its screen recording grant, and every
copy of such a build left on disk can end up holding it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
